{"surah": 103, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلْعَصْرِ ", "translation": "By time,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْعَصْرِ", "translit": "ِrْṣَʿعْlٱَw", "root": "عصر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ ", "translation": "Indeed, mankind is in loss,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خُسْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْsُhk", "root": "خسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ ", "translation": "Except for those who have believed and done righteous deeds and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَتَوَاصَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَṣāَwَtَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَتَوَاصَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَṣāَwَtَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِٱلصَّبْرِ", "translit": "ِrْbَّṣlٱِb", "root": "صبر"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "اهتدى وقوله تعالى والعصر إن الإنسان لفي خسر إلا الذين آمنوا وعملوا الصالحات وقوله تعالى وإن منكم إلا واردها كان على ربك حتما مقضيا {ثم قال} ثم ننجي الذين اتقوا وقوله تعالى ومن يعص الله ورسوله فإن له نار جهنم وكل آية ذكر الله عز وجل العمل الصالح فيها مقرونا بالإيمان وقوله تعالى ومن يقتل مؤمنا متعمدا فجزاؤه جهنم خالدا فيها وهذه العمومات أيضا مخصوصة بدليل قوله تعالى ويغفر ما دون ذلك لمن يشاء فينبغي أن تبقى له مشيئة في مغفرة ما سوى الشرك وكذلك قوله صلى الله عليه وسلم يخرج من النار من كان في قلبه مثقال ذرة من إي", "english": "He was asked, \"Which deed is most excellent?\" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"Islam.\" It was then asked, \"Which aspect of Islam is most excellent?\" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"Faith (Īmān).\" This is evidence for both the distinction (ikhtilāf) between the two terms and their overlap (tadākhul). This usage is the most consistent with the conventions of the language, because faith is a deed among deeds, and it is the most excellent of them. Islam is submission (taslīm), whether by the heart, by the tongue, or by the limbs. The most excellent of these is that which is by the heart, which is the assent (taṣdīq) that is called faith. Using the two terms in a way that indicates distinction, overlap, or even complete synonymy (tarāduf) is all within the bounds of metaphorical usage (tajawwuz) in the language.", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "section_title_ar": "Section 99", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 99: On the Distinction, Overlap, and Synonymy of Faith (Īmān) and Submission (Islām), and Their Worldly and Otherworldly Judgments", "section_index": 99, "anchors": "- Root: ايم (A-Y-M)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of remaining unmarried, or a state of being without a spouse; extended metaphorically to describe one who is solitary or without support.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الأيامى: جمع أيم، وهي المرأة التي لا بعل لها... والحرب مأيمة، أي: يفرق بين الزوج والزوجة.\" The root carries the sense of separation or a state of lacking union, which informs the theological discussion of what constitutes the essential bond of faith.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage denotes the state of being unmarried; metaphorical (Majaz) usage extends to anything that separates or leaves one bereft. This distinction between literal and metaphorical application is central to the chapter's method.\n- Root: قلب (Q-L-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn, overturn, or transform a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه... والانقلاب: الانصراف.\" The heart (qalb) is so named for its constant fluctuation and turning. In theological terms, it is the seat of taṣdīq (assent), the immaterial faculty of cognition and conviction.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage is physical turning; metaphorical (Majaz) usage is \"قلب الأمور\" — to deliberate, scrutinize, and manage affairs. This supports the distinction between the heart's internal act of assent and the external acts of the limbs.\n- Root: عمل (ʿ-A-M-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Any deed or action performed with purpose and intent.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العمل: كل فعل يكون من الحيوان بقصد، فهو أخص من الفعل.\" Work is more specific than mere action, as it implies deliberate, intentional agency. It is used for both righteous and sinful deeds, and is the external manifestation of internal conviction.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage refers to physical labor or deeds. The chapter explores whether \"work\" is an integral part of the reality of faith or a separate, consequent requirement.\n- Root: صدق (S-D-Q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To be truthful, to speak the truth, to verify.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الصدق والكذب أصلهما في القول... ولا يكونان بالقصد الأول إلا في القول.\" Truth and falsehood are primarily properties of speech and reports. Taṣdīq (assent) is the heart's affirmation of the truth of a report, which is the core reality of Īmān.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage is truthful speech; metaphorical (Majaz) usage is \"صادق الحملة\" — one who is true and firm in battle or resolve. This shows that taṣdīq is not merely verbal but a firm, internal resolution.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication). This rule governs how restriction (ḥaṣr) is achieved in Arabic, often through particles like \"innamā\" or through contextual specification (takhṣīṣ). The chapter's core argument hinges on how terms like Īmān and Islām are semantically restricted, expanded, or made synonymous through contextual usage (majāz), requiring precise parsing of the predicate and its scope.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وعمل صالحا ثم اهتدى وقوله تعالى والعصر إن الإنسان لفي خسر إلا الذين آمنوا وعملوا الصالحات وتواصوا بالحق وتواصوا بالصبر ذكر أربعة شروط وحيث اقتصر ذكر شرطا جامعا فقال تعالى إن رحمة الله قريب من المحسنين فالإحسان يجمع الكل وهكذا من يتصفح القرآن من أوله إلى آخره ومن فهم ذلك فجدير بأن يكون حاله الخشية والحزن ولذلك قال الحسن والله ما أصبح اليوم عبد يتلو القرآن يؤمن به إلا كثر حزنه وقل فرحه وكثر بكاؤه وقل ضحكه وكثر نصبه وشغله وقلت راحته وبطالته وقال وهيب بن الورد نظرنا في هذه الأحاديث والمواعظ فلم نجد شيئا أرق للقلوب ولا أشد استجلابا للحزن من قراءة القرآن وتفهمه وتدبره فتأ", "english": "[Root: ذكر]\n  • Al-Raghib (Al-Mufradat): \"الذكر: حضور الشيء القلب أو القول، ويكون تارة بالقلب وتارة باللسان، والذكر باللسان تارة يكون حضور المعنى وبعده، وقد يقال: ذكرته إذا جرى على لسانه وإن لم يحضره قلبه، والذكر بالقلب هو حضور المعنى، قال تعالى: ولا تطع من أغفلنا قلبه عن ذكرنا [الكهف/ 28]\"\n  • Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Haqiqah/Literal): \"ذكرت الشيء: نطقت به أو استحضرته بقلبك. وذكرت فلانا بخير وشر. واذكروا الله ذكرا كثيرا. والذكر: الشرف والصيت، قال تعالى: وإنه لذكر لك ولقومك [الزخرف/ 44]\"\n  • Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"الذكر: الكتاب الذي فيه تذكير الناس، قال تعالى: وأنزلنا إليك الذكر لتبين للناس ما نزل إليهم [النحل/ 44]، والذكر: القرآن، قال تعالى: إنا نحن نزلنا الذكر وإنا له لحافظون [الحجر/ 9]\"", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "section_title_ar": "Section 229", "section_title_en": "Section 229", "section_index": 229, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 1667]], "2": [[1, 350, 1439], [2, 1439, 3306], [3, 3306, 4350], [4, 4350, 5304]], "3": [[1, 400, 1063], [2, 1063, 1886], [3, 1886, 2979], [4, 2979, 4116], [5, 4116, 5384], [6, 5384, 6841], [7, 6841, 7642], [8, 7642, 9099], [9, 9099, 10094]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 250, 2683]], "2": [[1, 350, 1777], [2, 1777, 4224], [3, 4224, 5592], [4, 5592, 6843]], "3": [[1, 400, 1686], [2, 1686, 3283], [3, 3283, 5403], [4, 5403, 7608], [5, 7608, 10068], [6, 10068, 12895], [7, 12895, 14450], [8, 14450, 17277], [9, 17277, 19208]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 230, 1550]], "2": [[1, 330, 1369], [2, 1369, 3365], [3, 3365, 4466], [4, 4466, 5460]], "3": [[1, 460, 1349], [2, 1349, 2388], [3, 2388, 4056], [4, 4056, 5748], [5, 5748, 7207], [6, 7207, 9418], [7, 9418, 10292], [8, 10292, 12503], [9, 12503, 13580]]}, "abdulbasit_warsh": {"103:1": [[1, 400, 1310]], "103:2": [[1, 400, 965], [2, 1045, 1955], [3, 2035, 2600], [4, 2680, 3245]], "103:3": [[1, 400, 965], [2, 1045, 1840], [3, 1920, 2830], [4, 2910, 3820], [5, 3900, 4810], [6, 4890, 5915], [7, 5995, 6790], [8, 6870, 7895], [9, 7975, 8885]]}}, "letterTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"103:1": [{"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 0, "char": "و", "grapheme": "وَ", "start": 250, "end": 587, "duration": 337, "peakTime": 418}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ٱ", "grapheme": "ٱ", "start": 587, "end": 654, "duration": 67, "peakTime": 620}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 2, "char": "ل", "grapheme": "لْ", "start": 654, "end": 879, "duration": 225, "peakTime": 766}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 3, "char": "ع", "grapheme": "عَ", "start": 879, "end": 1149, "duration": 270, "peakTime": 1014}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 4, "char": "ص", "grapheme": "صْ", "start": 1149, "end": 1441, "duration": 292, "peakTime": 1295}, {